  "lineage": "Congregational singing of the Awakening movement (herännäisyys), the Pietist revival within the Finnish Lutheran church associated with the lay leader Paavo Ruotsalainen, whose followers are known as körttiläiset. At seurat gatherings and the annual Herättäjäjuhlat summer festival, hymns from the movement’s own book Siionin virret are sung in a markedly slow, drawn-out congregational style, separate from the Laestadian movement and its songbooks.",
